From 75548e30512ebdcd0cd9a32928d9694a1598e20d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Lukschander <oliver.lukschander@golf.at>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:01:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Generalize and clean up: the USB4 DP tunnel now works with
 zero flags

The DP tunnel is confirmed working end to end on real hardware (a real
2560x1440 picture on the external monitor over the OWC Thunderbolt 5 hub
+ Synaptics VMM7100 adapter), the culmination of candidates 0136-0142
this session. This commit removes every diagnostic-only addition made
purely to investigate the remaining issues, and every module_param gate
that was either confirmed dead scaffolding or a redundant opt-in layered
on top of scoping that was already hardware-precise -- so the driver now
needs no special module options at all on this hardware.

Removed entirely (all part of the pre-0127 "native DPIN0" single-purpose
proof of concept, fully superseded by the real tunnel-routing mechanism):
- usb4_native_dpin, usb4_protocol_probe, dcp_usb4_native_route() and the
  possible_crtcs exclusion it drove in apple_probe_typec_ports() (this
  exclusion was actively excluding dcpext0's CRTC bit from the tunnel
  connector's encoder, which is exactly why every atomic commit for it
  failed the generic encoder/CRTC pairing check with EINVAL before ever
  reaching a driver-level hook -- root-caused via two rounds of stale
  test-environment config that kept these "diagnostic" flags set to 1
  since candidate 0129, candidates 0140/0142).
- dpin_native and apple_usb4_dpin0_set_active() (drivers/thunderbolt/
  apple.c) -- an orphaned, single-caller-free duplicate of the real,
  generalized apple_dpin_set_active() a few hundred lines below it.
- usb4_defer_bringup and the whole deferred-bringup/frame-snapshot
  mechanism in the crossbar driver (t602x_right_dpin0_bring_up(),
  apple_dpxbar_right_dpin0_bring_up(), apple_dpxbar_right_frame_snapshot(),
  apple_dpxbar_is_typec_crossbar(), and their struct fields).

Generalized to unconditional, permanent behavior (removed the opt-in
flag, kept the logic):
- usb4_route_prefer_fixed_diag -> apple_dcp_tb_dp_tunnel()'s route
  scoring now always prefers a pipeline with a fixed output (dcpext0)
  for a Type-C tunnel route. Extensive hardware testing this session
  found dcpext1 (Type-C only, the "obvious" choice) never completes a
  real link for a tunnel target -- DCP firmware accepts request_display
  but never issues another apcall, a firmware-internal decision with no
  driver-source asymmetry to explain or fix it. dcpext0 reaches a full
  real AUX/DPCD link and, with the fixes below, a working picture.
- usb4_tunnel_clock (drivers/phy/apple/atc.c) and dp_bw_grant (drivers/
  thunderbolt/tunnel.c) -- both already gated on
  of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j416s") plus specific port/PHY
  compatibility checks; the extra opt-in flag was redundant. (
  dp_video_counter, a genuine self-described optional debugfs
  diagnostic, is left untouched -- not scaffolding.)

Removed (fired on every atomic commit or every frame in production use,
added purely to investigate this session's mysteries, no longer needed):
- apple_plane_atomic_check()'s per-exit dev_info() calls (plane.c is now
  byte-identical to its pre-session state).
- dcp_hotplug()'s and dcp_crtc_atomic_modeset()'s crtc-state diagnostics
  (iomfb.c).
- dcp_crtc_atomic_check()'s per-commit diagnostic (dcp.c).
- apple_probe_typec_ports()'s possible_crtcs-computation diagnostic
  (apple_drv.c).

Net: -556/+43 lines across 10 files. Built and verified: all four
affected modules (appledrm, mux-apple-display-crossbar,
thunderbolt/thunderbolt_apple, phy-apple-atc) rebuild cleanly with no
new warnings (one pre-existing, unrelated unused-function warning in
apple.c predates this session entirely, confirmed via git show HEAD).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
